WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:04.440
so I was sitting with my friends on the
stairs of a fountain at the center of my

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:08.519
favorite square and Rome where I used to
gather with my friends to have a few

00:00:08.519 --> 00:00:13.559
laughs and drinks when all of a sudden I
heard this loud burp behind me and I

00:00:13.559 --> 00:00:18.510
turned and I asked: "who's that?!" and "that's one loud burp", and actually the person

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:22.439
who had done that was a girl, an American
girl who herself asked me: "are you

00:00:22.439 --> 00:00:26.760
American?" and I told her that I was Italian and that was really surprising and

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:30.720
we started chatting and I actually got
to know one of my best friends, who was

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:36.570
sitting next to her - that is Garrett - and
this is one of the surprising and

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:40.860
unexpected ways in which languages can
actually change and revolutionize your life

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:47.100
Imagine a prism: when light hits
that prism you will see its basic

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:51.329
components.YOU are that light and
languages are like that prison which

00:00:51.329 --> 00:00:56.219
help you show and broaden literally the
facets of your personality. Think about

00:00:56.219 --> 00:01:00.149
it for a second: when you speak a foreign
language, your facial features, the

00:01:00.149 --> 00:01:04.140
thoughts that you think, your actions,
your reactions are all slightly

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:09.299
different than when you speak your
mother tongue and we only have ONE life.

00:01:09.299 --> 00:01:14.130
it's true but it's also true that the
more languages you speak, the more lives

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:18.799
we can live within one live span.

00:01:19.759 --> 00:01:24.420
Learning a language is a little bit like
running a marathon: you learn a lot of

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:29.520
valuable life lessons by doing that. For
example, you learn the importance of

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:34.200
being humble, the importance of knowing
yourself, knowing when to speed up and

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:38.570
when to slow down. The importance of
trial-and-error. Daily routine,

00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:44.640
regularity, habits, belief in yourself,
and I have learned these life lessons

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:48.450
through language and have carried them
over into other fields and domains of

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:53.909
life. For example I have learned how to
become more productive, how to develop

00:01:53.909 --> 00:01:59.640
good sleeping and eating habits. So, it
has brought about a change in my life

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:04.659
overall.

00:02:04.659 --> 00:02:08.780
Traveling is in and of itself an amazing
experience it doesn't matter where you

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:12.620
go and it doesn't matter how many
languages you speak. But if you speak the

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:15.770
local language or you speak many
languages, it changes, it completely

00:02:15.770 --> 00:02:20.209
changes your experience. Back in the days when I used to live in Paris, I used to

00:02:20.209 --> 00:02:26.060
carry out this social experiment: I used
to walk into bars speaking English and

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:30.110
asking things around and the reaction
was obviously very cold. But then - and

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:33.950
within the same day - I used to go to
other bars and speak in French and the

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:38.959
reaction was completely different which
goes to show that human beings all

00:02:38.959 --> 00:02:43.430
across the globe have the same desires,
the same actions, the same thoughts the

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:47.060
same reactions and only apparently we
are different through the barrier of

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:51.170
language. Every language that you learn
is like a key that unlocks a new pathway

00:02:51.170 --> 00:03:00.500
to human experience. When you go to the
gym and you see all these big guys you

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:03.709
realize that the reason why their
muscles are so big is because they work

00:03:03.709 --> 00:03:09.049
out. Differently from the muscles,
actually we cannot see the brain itself

00:03:09.049 --> 00:03:14.900
but the brain works in exactly the same
way: if you make your brain work, your

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:19.070
brain will become smoother, leaner and
more efficient and through language

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:23.060
learning that can happen very fast.
Language learning has AMAZING benefits

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:26.480
in terms of learning other
languages, for example when I started

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:30.950
learning Dutch after learning German, or
learning Portuguese after learning

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:34.940
Spanish, I was astounded at the rate at
which I was acquiring these languages

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:39.019
which is natural because these languages
were similar to the languages I already

00:03:39.019 --> 00:03:43.670
knew .But in general the more languages
you learn, the more cognitive benefits

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:49.489
you reap. For example I am more
socially and culturally aware, I am a

00:03:49.489 --> 00:03:54.350
better imitator, I'm a better listener, I
think I'm a more empathic person, and a

00:03:54.350 --> 00:04:00.470
more caring person. Imagine casting a net into the ocean: the bigger and the better

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:04.880
the net, the more fish you're gonna get. Now think about all these social events

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:09.350
you have participated in: when you speak
another language and you meet a person

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:12.769
who speaks that language, even a few
words in that language can make a

00:04:12.769 --> 00:04:18.260
difference because you're establishing a
direct, natural and emphatic relationship

00:04:18.260 --> 00:04:20.959
with that person,
and that makes all the difference. When

00:04:20.959 --> 00:04:25.669
it comes to establishing connections,
making long-lasting relationships,

00:04:25.669 --> 00:04:32.300
friendships and even love, which takes us
to the next point: so this this is what

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:37.250
happened 2017 in Prague. I was sitting with
my friends at a hostel and then we

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:41.690
started talking to these three French
girls, who were surprised that I spoke French

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:46.520
and that I spoke it well, and then thanks to
that I actually established a connection

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:50.720
I got to know her better and eventually
she would become my girlfriend now the

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:55.190
interesting thing is that speaking
French not only helped me connect, make

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:59.630
this connection, but it hope also helped
me solidify and cement this relationship

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:04.340
because the quality of the relationship
the empathy between the two of us - that

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:10.880
was different and imagine like speaking
languages like having a little Cupid

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:13.940
shooting the arrow between you and
another person

00:05:13.940 --> 00:05:18.560
it actually makes love thrive and I've
learned that, you know, the important

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:24.680
message that love is the same universal
message for everyone but it's wrapped up

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:28.550
and coded in different cultures and
different cultural codes and to unlock

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:35.419
that you need to speak foreign languages.
Back in the days in 2010 when I moved to

00:05:35.419 --> 00:05:40.130
Paris, I didn't know exactly what to do
but I knew that I had a big passion for

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:43.880
languages and eventually languages caught up with me and found me and I

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:47.930
started working with languages so I told
myself "bingo, I do what I love and I love

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:52.100
what I do but you don't have to
necessarily work with languages, meaning,

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:56.270
you have to be a translator or you have
to be an interpreter, you can be whatever

00:05:56.270 --> 00:06:00.500
you want. But if you speak languages if
you have a good command of languages,

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:06.229
that can actually make your career
improve and you can find jobs much more

00:06:06.229 --> 00:06:10.729
easily because with languages you not
only acquire words and sentences but you

00:06:10.729 --> 00:06:16.010
also acquire a command of the cultural
structures and cultural codes underlying

00:06:16.010 --> 00:06:20.990
negotiations or other things that can
actually make your life and the life of

00:06:20.990 --> 00:06:25.669
the company or the organization you work with much easier and smoother.

00:06:25.669 --> 00:06:29.410
Imagine speaking languages like having a toolbox: the more languages you speak, the

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:36.640
more tools you have to do whatever you
want. The bottom line of all this is that

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:42.190
learning a language or many languages is
never ever a waste of time it's not just

00:06:42.190 --> 00:06:46.420
a matter of learning new sounds or new
sentences or new words

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:51.550
it's about being more: being a more
competent person and more socially and

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:56.140
culturally aware person. In the end it's
about being more empathic, more

00:06:56.140 --> 00:07:01.210
understanding and more humane, and we
need this in this globalized world. So if

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:05.860
you're thinking of learning a language
just do it NOW, because it will have a

00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:10.960
huge impact not only on your life but on
the life of those who surround you.

